        "original_id": "879db62c-c247-52de-89cf-e7e60fd8ea9e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Samuel Rickards\n- Organizations: Church of England, Trinity Episcopal Church (Houghton, Michigan)\n- Movements: Oxford Movement, Anglo-Catholicism\n- Roles: clergyman, writer\n- Topics: devotional literature\n\nFacts:\n- Samuel Rickards was born in 1796 and died in 1865.\n- Samuel Rickards was a Church of England clergyman.\n- Samuel Rickards opposed the Oxford Movement.\n- Samuel Rickards wrote devotional literature.\n- The Oxford Movement was a movement of High Church members of the Church of England.\n- The Oxford Movement eventually developed into Anglo-Catholicism.\n- Trinity Episcopal Church in Houghton, Michigan has a philosophy built on the Oxford Movement.",
